{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "126bb660-5354-5e40-b211-86e92adebade"/*PhysicsVolumesExample*/,
  "Description": "Any volume becomes a collider through [VolumeToMesh]. On the left, the bunny is loaded with [LoadVdb], made coarser with [VolumeResample] and scaled down; on the right, a bowl is carved out of a block with [VolumeCsg]. Balls rain on both.\n\nAKA: vdb, nanovdb, openvdb, level set, voxel collider, csg, bunny\n\nTips\n- Playback must run for the simulation to advance; press Reset on the World to start over.\n- A coarser VoxelSize gives fewer triangles and a cheaper collider.\n- A volume that changes rebuilds the collider, so animate it sparingly.",
